        "article_text_excerpt": "Weather in the weekend will be cloudy and in some parts of the country rain will prevail up to the begining of next week. Friday will be mostly cloudy, with a widespread band of precipitation moving across Latvia from the southwest during the night, bringing rain to the entire country, according to the Latvian Environment, Geology and Meteorology Centre. Light to moderate southeasterly and easterly winds will prevail, gradually shifting to southerly and southwesterly directions from midday, beginning in western Latvia. Overnight temperatures will fall to between +7°C and +11°C, although some eastern areas could see temperatures drop to +4°C to +6°C where skies clear. During the day, temperatures will rise to between +9°C and +13°C. Saturday will bring variable cloud cover. Light rain is possible in parts of eastern Latvia overnight, but daytime conditions will be mostly dry. Light to moderate southerly winds are expected. During the morning and late morning, fog will develop across man",
